-- title:
--   A-integral q-expansions lie in the ∞̄-chart
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` whose residue field has characteristic $p$. Let $\Gamma$ be a chart context `ChartCtx p A`, that is: modular polynomial data for $p$ together with the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \bmod p = (X'^p - X)(X' - X^p)$ for it, integrality of the Hecke $\bar\alpha$- and $\bar\beta$-maps at level $1$ and prime $p$, a place specialisation $P$ from places of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in the base-changed modular function field of level $1$ to places of the residue field of $A$ in `modularFunctionFieldC` of level $1$, a level-one prolongation pair $R$ for $P$, a set $S_1$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a finite set $W_n$ of places of the residue-field modular function field shown to enumerate exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces p 1`, finiteness of the supersingular $j$-set with cardinality `mAnnuli p`, and a `ChartFstSupply` datum for $R$ and $S_1$. Let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot p$, and suppose every coefficient $f_n$, $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, of $f$ as a Laurent series lies in $A$. Then $f$ belongs to the valuation subring `integers` of the component chart `infChart Γ`, the first chart attached to $\Gamma.R$ by `chartFst` with data $\Gamma.S_1$, $\Gamma.W_n$ and $\Gamma.\mathrm{supply}$.
--
--   This is the integrality half of the $q$-expansion principle for the $\bar\infty$-chart of the multiplicative covering of $X_0(p)$ at $p$: the Gauss prolongation of $A$ along the $q$-expansion at $\infty$ contains every modular function whose $q$-expansion has coefficients in $A$. It is part of the exported interface of that chart, used in the construction of unimodular family data and of a uniform multiplicative covering for primes $p \geq 5$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_MultCovering_mem_infChart_integers_of_forall_coeff_mem.lean

